Let \( \mathcal{T}_r \) denote legitimate tradition:

\[
\mathcal{T}_r := 
\begin{array}{l}
\text{Tradition that:} \\
\quad \text{Has been witnessed over time} \\
\quad \text{Is grounded in lived experience} \\
\quad \text{Is adapted and refined} \\
\quad \text{Serves the continuity of the whole} \\
\quad \text{Is maintained by fidelity, not fear}
\end{array}
\]

**Theorem 5: Organic Hierarchy Is Grounded in Tradition**

\[
\mathcal{O}_h \to \mathcal{T}_r
\]

**Proof:**

1. Organic hierarchy is not invented—it emerges.
2. Emergence occurs over time.
3. Emergence is witnessed and recorded in tradition.
4. Tradition provides continuity and stability.
5. Therefore, organic hierarchy is grounded in tradition.

**Corollary 5: Tradition Is the Witness of Emergence**

\[
\mathcal{T}_r = \text{Witness}(\text{Emergence})
\]

Tradition is not dead—it is living. It is the accumulated wisdom of those who have witnessed the hierarchy and found it legitimate.

