## 7. The Dependence of Law and Tradition

**Theorem 6: Law and Tradition Are Dependent on Each Other**

\[
\mathcal{L}_w \iff \mathcal{T}_r
\]

**Proof:**

| Aspect | Law | Tradition |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Nature | Formal | Informal |
| Function | Articulation | Witness |
| Source | Consent | Emergence |
| Maintenance | Fidelity | Fidelity |
| Failure | Loss of consent | Loss of meaning |

**Corollary 6: Neither Is Sufficient Alone**

\[
\mathcal{L}_w \to \mathcal{T}_r \quad \land \quad \mathcal{T}_r \to \mathcal{L}_w
\]

Law without tradition is arbitrary. Tradition without law is unarticulated. Organic hierarchy requires both.

