**Theorem 7: Organic Hierarchy Is a Dependence Structure**

\[
\mathcal{O}_h = \text{Structure}(\mathcal{D}_p)
\]

**The Organic Hierarchy:**

| Level | Role | Dependence | Basis |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Leaders** | Serve, guide, protect | Dependent on consent | Fidelity |
| **Institutions** | Articulate, mediate | Dependent on law and tradition | Consent |
| **Community** | Live, work, witness | Dependent on leadership and institutions | Tradition |
| **Law** | Formalize consent | Dependent on community and tradition | Witnessing |
| **Tradition** | Witness emergence | Dependent on community and law | Lived experience |

**Corollary 7: The Structure Is Cyclical, Not Linear**

\[
\mathcal{O}_h = \text{Cycle}(\text{Service} \to \text{Consent} \to \text{Law} \to \text{Tradition} \to \text{Service})
\]

Organic hierarchy is not a top-down command structure. It is a cyclical dependence structure—each level serves and depends on the others.

